  "description": "Verification of equation-audit entry E-33: the wall-truncation response of the E-25 finite-cylinder elliptic problem -L5 psi1 = omega1 with psi1(R,z)=0, for a compactly supported source. Axial modes L_z in {1,2,4,8,16,32} at m=1 plus one exactly z-independent case sweep kR from 0.196 to 50.3, crossing the E-33(c) transition at kR ~ 1. Every wall radius shares the radial spacing, so the core nodes are bitwise identical and the core differences are exact nodewise comparisons.",
  "experiment": "wall_truncation_scaling_v1",
  "interpretation": "This measures how the solution of THIS discretization of THIS finite-cylinder problem moves when the artificial outer wall is moved, and checks that the movement obeys the closed form E-33 derives. It is not a continuum bound, not a whole-space result, and not singularity evidence. Its programmatic content is the opposite of reassuring: the k=0 component's truncation error falls only like R^-2, so approximating the whole space by a large finite cylinder converges only algebraically.",
